  "content": {
    "title": "Dunkin' is giving away 1 million free coffees again. How to get yours",
    "text": "April 20, 2026Updated April 21, 2026, 12:14 p.m. ETAfter giving away over a million free coffees on April Fools' Day, Dunkin' is at it again.The coffee chain is giving away another million coffees on Tuesday, April 21, the company confirmed to USA TODAY.Dunkin' Rewards members can use promo code \"FREECOFFEE1\" in their Dunkin' app beginning 9 a.m. local time on April 21 to redeem the offer, while supplies last. The company teased the promotion on social media on Friday, April 17.The chain also told USA TODAY consumers have seven days after getting the offer to redeem it. Cold brew and extra-large hot coffees are not included as part of the promotion, and there is a limit of one per customer.Dunkin' unveils spring menu, launches new canned coffeeThe free coffee giveaway comes on the heels of Dunkin' unveiling its spring menu, which includes several banana-flavored drinks as well as the return of the $6 meal deal.The coffee chain also recently announced the launch of Dunkin' Double 15 oz. cans \"that bring fans more of the smooth iced espresso taste they love in a format built to power busy days.\"Dunkin’ Double contains the equivalent of two espresso shots, Dunkin said, and comes in three fan-favorite flavors including original, café mocha and salted caramel.Dunkin' Double joined the brand's lineup of ready-to-drink beverages, which includes bottled iced coffees. The canned beverages are available to purchase at major retailers, including Walmart, Kroger, Publix, QuikTrip and Amazon.Contributing: Mike Snider, USA TODAY; Saman Shafiq, USA TODAYGabe Hauari is a national trending news reporter at USA TODAY. You can follow him on X @GabeHauari or email him at Gdhauari@gannett.com.",
